# Line-ending policy.
#
# This matters more than usual here: the release workflow runs `./gradlew` on a Linux runner.
# A `gradlew` that arrives with CRLF line endings fails there with `bad interpreter: No such
# file or directory` — a confusing error that points at the interpreter rather than at the
# line endings that caused it.
#
# So text is normalised to LF in the repository, and only the Windows batch files keep CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.bat text eol=crlf
gradlew text eol=lf

# The Gradle wrapper jar is binary; without this git would try to normalise it and corrupt it.
*.jar binary
*.jks binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
